 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Overhead:** Storing the bit length for every voxel or block can incur substantial overhead relative to the value bits themselves [S2].
-*   **Precision:** Ensure that the bit length $n$ is sufficient to represent the maximum residual without overflow [G].
-*   **Structure Choice:** The choice between block-based and quadtree-based partitioning affects compression ratio and decoding complexity [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Metadata Overhead:** VBLE alone incurs overhead because the bit length for each voxel must be stored. This is usually mitigated by combining VBLE with RLE [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Precision:** The method assumes integer or quantized data. Floating-point data requires preprocessing (e.g., prediction and conversion to integers) before VBLE can be applied effectively [S1, unofficial].
